.TH NGINX2ROOT 1 "November 2026" "nginx2root 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nginx2root \- audit nginx for HTTP/2 weaknesses and nginx-to-root privilege paths
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nginx2root
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nginx2root
is a read-only auditor for nginx installations. It reads the configuration that
nginx actually loads, inspects local permissions and processes, and optionally
probes the live TLS listener. It reports findings with a severity, a concrete
fix, and a reference.
.PP
The audit covers six groups: environment, HTTP/2, TLS, nginx-to-root privilege
paths, configuration flaws, and network/listener state. A built-in advisory
table adds feature-gated CVE checks with branch-aware version matching.
.PP
The tool never writes to nginx, reloads it, or exploits a vulnerability. It is
intended for a VPS, a home server, or a laptop running nginx.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Config source
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Use \fIPATH\fR as the nginx configuration (passed to \fBnginx \-c\fR).
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-dump " \fIPATH\fR"
Read an existing \fBnginx \-T\fR dump instead of the local installation. This
enables offline mode: file-permission and listener checks are skipped.
.TP
.BI \-\-nginx\-version " \fIVERSION\fR"
Version to use for CVE matching in offline mode, for example \fB1.31.9\fR.
.SS Checks
.TP
.B \-\-no\-live
Skip TLS, ALPN, certificate, and HTTP probes.
.TP
.B \-\-live
Force live probes even when \fB\-\-dump\fR is used.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " \fIHOST\fR"
Host to probe (default \fB127.0.0.1\fR).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIPORT\fR"
TLS port to probe (default \fB443\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " \fISECONDS\fR"
Probe timeout in seconds (default \fB5\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-domains " \fIN\fR"
Maximum number of \fBserver_name\fR values to probe (default \fB25\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sudo
Never try \fBsudo \-n\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " \fILIST\fR"
Run only the listed check IDs or prefixes, comma-separated. For example
\fBH2,TLS\fR or \fBROOT\-00\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " \fILIST\fR"
Skip the listed check IDs or prefixes, comma-separated.
.SS Output
.TP
.BI \-\-format " \fIFORMAT\fR"
Output format: \fBtext\fR (default) or \fBjson\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Alias for \fB\-\-format json\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-severity " \fILEVEL\fR"
Only print findings at or above \fILEVEL\fR:
\fBcritical\fR, \fBhigh\fR, \fBmedium\fR, \fBlow\fR, or \fBinfo\fR.
This filters display only; it does not change the exit code.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " \fILEVEL\fR"
Exit with status 1 when a finding at or above \fILEVEL\fR exists. Accepts the
same levels plus \fBnone\fR. The default is \fBhigh\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colour.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only actionable findings.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also show passing and skipped checks.
.SS Other
.TP
.B \-\-list\-checks
List every check and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-cves
List the built-in advisory table and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Run internal unit tests and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No findings at or above the \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR level.
.TP
.B 1
At least one finding at or above the \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR level.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or environment error.
.TP
.B 3
The nginx configuration could not be read or parsed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
Default configuration when no \fB\-\-config\fR is given.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/nginx2root
Default install location.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/nginx2root.1
Manual page installed by \fBinstall.sh\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a full audit as root:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo nginx2root
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fail CI on medium findings and emit JSON:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo nginx2root \-\-format json \-\-fail\-on medium > audit.json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Audit only HTTP/2 and TLS:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo nginx2root \-\-only H2,TLS
.EE
.RE
.PP
Audit a dump from another host:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
nginx2root \-\-dump nginx\-T.txt \-\-nginx\-version 1.31.9 \-\-no\-live
.EE
.RE
.PP
Probe a non-default listener:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo nginx2root \-\-host 127.0.0.1 \-\-port 8443
.EE
.RE
.SH SEVERITY
.TP
.B critical
A direct path to root or host compromise. Fix immediately.
.TP
.B high
Serious exposure or a reliable privilege-escalation primitive.
.TP
.B medium
A meaningful weakness that needs a second condition or local access.
.TP
.B low
A hardening gap or defense-in-depth issue.
.TP
.B info
Context, inventory, or a best-practice suggestion.
.SH SAFETY
The audit is read-only. Probes connect only to the host and port given by
\fB\-\-host\fR and \fB\-\-port\fR, using \fBserver_name\fR values from the
configuration. Do not run the tool against hosts you do not own.
.SH NOTES
Root is required for complete permission and process inspection. Without root,
the tool still parses the configuration and runs most checks, and it tries
\fBsudo \-n\fR once when available.
.PP
CVE checks require a known nginx version and an enabled affected feature.
The advisory table is current as of 2026-11-20; update \fBCVE_DATA\fR in the
script when new advisories are published.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nginx (8),
.BR nginx \-T ,
.BR openssl (1)
.PP
Project documentation: \fIdocs/checks.md\fR and \fIREADME.md\fR.
